<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Victor Emmanuel III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1869–1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Victor Emmanuel III of Italy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Victor Emmanuel III was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from 1900 to 1946. He appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a> prime minister in 1922 and accepted the titles Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1936 and King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a> in 1939 after Italian conquests. He dismissed Mussolini in 1943 but, discredited by his long cooperation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascism">Fascism</a>, abdicated in May 1946, shortly before a referendum abolished the monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-iii.jpg" alt="Victor Emmanuel III" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mario Nunes Vais · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vitorio_Emanuel_III_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
